        "description": "Axium Aster & Axium Bloom is Axium Infrastructure's combined manager-level investment in two Canadian long-term-care property portfolios. Axium's current portfolio materials report 26 operating facilities and 4,114 beds across Alberta and British Columbia, with cash flows supported by provincially licensed, regulated and funded long-term-care and continuing-care frameworks plus resident co-payments. Axium owns 92.5% of each portfolio; AgeCare owns the 7.5% balance and operates the facilities. Aster began in 2020 as a five-facility, 1,402-bed Alberta partnership at 80% Axium and 20% AgeCare. Bloom traces to the western tranche of the Revera-Axium joint venture that first closed in 2017; Revera sold its remaining 15% interest in certain Alberta and British Columbia homes to AgeCare in 2022. Individual homes are underlying assets, and the separately presented 16-home Ontario Axium Iris portfolio is outside this company boundary. No Axium exit or signed pending sale was identified through August 18, 2026.",
